  "generated_text": "1. A regular dodecagon has 12 vertices.\n2. To form a triangle, we need to choose 3 vertices out of 12.\n3. The number of ways to choose 3 vertices from 12 is given by the combination formula \\( \\binom{n}{k} \\ \\frac{n!}{k!(n-k)!} \\).\n\nHere, \\( n = 12 \\) and \\( k = 3 \\).\n\n\\[\n\\binom{12}{3} = \\frac{12!}{3!(12-3)!} = \\frac{12!}{3! \\cdot 9!}\n\\]\n\nSimplify the factorials:\n\n\\[\n\\binom{12}{3} = \\frac{12 \\times 11 \\times 10!}{3 \\times 2 \\times 1} = \\frac{12 \\times 11 \\times 10}{6} = \\frac{1320}{6} = 220\n\\]\n\nSo, the number of triangles that can be formed using the vertices of a regular decagon is \\boxed{220}.",
